// ============================================================================
// STUDENT PAGE DATA: blank sample
//
// Lines that start with // are comments. The page ignores them, so you can keep
// or delete them when you copy this file.
//
// ADD A NEW STUDENT (example: Maya Smith at caidenlee.com/mayasmith)
//   1. Copy this file to students/mayasmith.json and fill it in.
//      The file name must match the URL name exactly.
//      Use lowercase letters, numbers and dashes only.
//   2. Copy the folder adamnasser/ (at the top of the site) and rename the
//      copy to mayasmith/. Do not edit the index.html inside it. It is the
//      same for every student.
//   3. Pick a URL name that no other page on the site uses (not "tools",
//      "inbox", "f2l" and so on).
//   4. Commit and push. The page is live in about a minute.
//
// ADD A NEW SESSION FOR AN EXISTING STUDENT
//   1. Open students/<name>.json.
//   2. Copy one whole { ... } block inside "sessions", paste it as a new block,
//      and change the date and notes. Put a comma between blocks.
//   3. The newest date always shows first. Older sessions move into the
//      "Past Sessions" list automatically, so never delete old ones.
//   4. Each session has its own checklist, so new drills start unchecked.
//
// FIELD GUIDE
//   date      "YYYY-MM-DD". Required. Also identifies the session.
//   stats     Pills under the header. Add "sub" for a small second line and
//             "wide": true to make a pill span the full row.
//             The "Current Average" and "Goal" stats become the goal bar at
//             the top when both contain a number (for example "12.6" and
//             "Sub 10"). Otherwise they show as normal pills.
//   theme     The "Big Theme" banner: a title plus short points.
//   tabs      Usually Cross, F2L, Last Layer. Each has:
//               fix       "What to Fix" notes (plain text)
//               practice  "How to Practice" checklist. Each drill is either
//                         plain text, or an object with:
//                           text      the drill (required)
//                           note      small gray line under it (optional)
//                           link      a URL, or a site path like "/cross-trainer.html"
//                           linkText  the link's button label (default "Open")
//                           target    how much to do, shown as a badge,
//                                     like "25 solves" or "10 min"
//             Checklists clear themselves at the start of each new day.
//             Checking off every drill sets off confetti.
//
// PRACTICE LOG
//   Students log each practice day themselves on the page: drills checked,
//   minutes, their average and notes. Nothing to add here. The log is saved
//   on the student's own phone, so "Send to Caiden" is how you see it, and
//   "Back up" / "Restore" moves it to a new phone.
//
// Keep every value in "double quotes", and remember the comma between items.
// ============================================================================
{
  "name": "Student First Name",
  "sessions": [
    {
      "date": "2026-01-01",
      "stats": [
        { "label": "Current Average", "value": "" },
        { "label": "Goal", "value": "" },
        { "label": "PR Single", "value": "" },
        { "label": "Method / Knowledge", "value": "", "sub": "" }
      ],
      "theme": {
        "title": "",
        "points": ["", ""]
      },
      "tabs": [
        {
          "name": "Cross",
          "fix": [""],
          "practice": [
            "",
            { "text": "", "note": "", "link": "", "linkText": "", "target": "" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "F2L",
          "fix": [""],
          "practice": [""]
        },
        {
          "name": "Last Layer",
          "fix": [""],
          "practice": [""]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
